Template: hamnews/callsign
Type: string
Description: Your callsign:
 It becomes this news server's name: the Path: entry on every article it
 handles and the domain of its Message-IDs, so it must be unique on the net.
 Letters, digits and hyphens, e.g. kn6fln or kn6fln-pnc; no SSID and no
 leading or trailing hyphen. It is stored in lowercase.
 .
 Leave it empty to set pathhost and domain in /etc/hamnews/inn.conf by hand;
 hamnews will not start until they are set.

Template: hamnews/callsign-invalid
Type: error
Description: "${call}" is not a callsign
 Use letters, digits and hyphens only, with no SSID, no leading or trailing
 hyphen, and no other punctuation.
